tte-county"],["PRF calculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record for Fayette County runs 75 years, 1951 to 2025. On the middle of the county&rsquo;s grids, February to March came in under 90% of normal in 36 of those years. In 2025 on the middle, July to August came in at 52% of normal and November to December at 40%, while May to June ran 185%. In 2026 so far, January to February came in at 48% of normal on the middle.</p>"}
